## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design online, scalable PCA under latency and privacy constraints for a large IoT data stream, plus practical concerns about drift, imputation, and actionable loadings.

## Key Concepts

- Online/incremental PCA (e.g., incremental SVD, randomized SVD)
- Missing data handling in streaming PCA
- Privacy: secure aggregation or differential privacy on sufficient statistics
- Drift detection and adaptive component updates
- Mapping components to domain-specific fault rules with controlled FPR

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudocode: incremental update
function updatePCA(X_t, state){
  const X = impute(X_t);
  const [U,S,V] = incrementalSVD(X, state);
  state.update(U,S,V);
  return state;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you choose the number of components in changing fault modes?
- How would you benchmark latency vs. accuracy in production?

